msgstr "`DELETE /api/v1/labels/{name}` { #delete-labels-name }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid "Delete a label file (admin); its data file stays."
msgstr "Sildifaili kustutamine (admin); selle andmefail jääb alles."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 204 | Deleted |  |\n"
"| 400 | Not a name inside the labels folder | `invalid_field` |\n"
"| 404 | No such label | `label_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | Jobs of it wait or print (label_in_use), or another program's print holds the file | `label_in_use`, `label_locked` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 204 | Kustutatud |  |\n"
"| 400 | Pole nimi siltide kausta sees | `invalid_field` |\n"
"| 404 | Sellist silti pole | `label_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | Sildi töid ootab või prinditakse (label_in_use) või teise programmi print hoiab faili | `label_in_use`, `label_locked` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     -X DELETE \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/labels/asset-tag\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`POST /api/v1/data` { #post-data }"
msgstr "`POST /api/v1/data` { #post-data }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid ""
"Read a data file sent along (CSV, ODS, XLSX) as the app reads one: its rows "
"for data_rows; nothing is kept."
msgstr ""
"Päringuga kaasa saadetud andmefaili (CSV, ODS, XLSX) lugemine nii, nagu "
"rakendus seda loeb: selle read väljale data_rows; midagi ei salvestata."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid "Body fields:"
msgstr "Keha väljad:"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field | Type | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `content` | string | The file: CSV (any delimiter, UTF-8, UTF-16 or Windows-1252), ODS or XLSX, told apart by content. Pasted text is a CSV file. |\n"
"| `name` | string | The file's name, for messages. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | ODS, XLSX: the sheet (default the first). |\n"
"| `header` | boolean | false: the first row is data too; the columns are named A, B, C … default `true` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Väli | Tüüp | Tähendus |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `content` | string | Fail: CSV (mis tahes eraldaja, UTF-8, UTF-16 või Windows-1252), ODS või XLSX, eristatakse sisu järgi. Kleebitud tekst on CSV-fail. |\n"
"| `name` | string | Faili nimi teadete jaoks. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | ODS, XLSX: leht (vaikimisi esimene). |\n"
"| `header` | boolean | false: esimene rida on samuti andmed; veerud on nimega A, B, C … Vaikimisi `true` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | The rows |  |\n"
"| 400 | Invalid request | `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `not_json` |\n"
"| 422 | Not a table, damaged or empty | `data_problem` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | Read |  |\n"
"| 400 | Vigane päring | `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `not_json` |\n"
"| 422 | Pole tabel, on kahjustatud või tühi | `data_problem` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"name\": \"assets.csv\", \"content\": \"QXNzZXROdW1iZXIKMDAzMDAKMDAzMDEK\"}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/data\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`POST /api/v1/preview` { #post-preview }"
msgstr "`POST /api/v1/preview` { #post-preview }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid "The label filled in, as an image; nothing is printed."
msgstr "Täidetud silt pildina; midagi ei prindita."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field | Type | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `label` | string | Name of a label file in the labels folder (see GET /labels), subfolders with '/'; '`.tavletta`' may be left out. Either label or label_content. |\n"
"| `label_content` | object | Or the label itself, as the JSON of a `.tavletta` file, checked like a file that is opened. Its data file is ignored (send data_rows instead), its counter never saved. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | With `printers.toml` on the server: the printer's name (default: the default printer the token may use, or the only one). Without it: a printer model id, if not the label's own (the label is fitted as in the app). |\n"
"| `set` | object | Element name or variable name -> value, as `--set` on the command line; variables in a value are filled in; 'date' sets the moment `{=date}` and `{=time}` start from (ISO 8601). At most 1000 entries. |\n"
"| `set_literal` | object | Like set, but braces in a value are text, not variables. |\n"
"| `counter_start` | integer | The `{=counter}` of the first label; it goes up by the label's step with every label, copy and row. 0 to 999999999999999 |\n"
"| `data_rows` | array of object | Serial labels: one label per row, column name -> value; the label's `{Column}` placeholders take the values. Numbers are taken as text, null as an empty cell. At most 100000 rows, 1000 columns, 2000000 cells, 100000 characters a value. |\n"
"| `data_file` | string | Or a CSV, TSV, ODS or XLSX file in the labels folder. Without data_rows and data_file, the label's own data file is used if it lies beside the label in the labels folder. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | Sheet of the data file, the first by default. |\n"
"| `row` | integer | Data row to show, from 1. 1 to 100000; default `1` |\n"
"| `format` | `\"png\"` \\| `\"json\"` | 'json': width, height, warnings and the PNG in base64. default `\"png\"` |\n"
"| `view` | `\"preview\"` \\| `\"printer\"` | 'printer': the image as the printer gets it (turned, in its colours). default `\"preview\"` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Väli | Tüüp | Tähendus |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `label` | string | Sildifaili nimi siltide kaustas (vaata GET /labels), alamkaustad märgiga '/'; '`.tavletta`' võib ära jätta. Kas label või label_content. |\n"
"| `label_content` | object | Või silt ise, `.tavletta`-faili JSON-ina, kontrollitud nagu avatav fail. Selle andmefaili ignoreeritakse (saada selle asemel data_rows), selle loendurit ei salvestata kunagi. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | Serveris oleva `printers.toml`-iga: printeri nimi (vaikimisi: vaikeprinter, mida token tohib kasutada, või ainus). Ilma selleta: printerimudeli id, kui see ei ole sildi enda oma (silt sobitatakse nagu rakenduses). |\n"
"| `set` | object | Elemendi nimi või muutuja nimi -> väärtus, nagu `--set` käsureal; väärtuses olevad muutujad täidetakse; 'date' seab hetke, millest `{=date}` ja `{=time}` alustavad (ISO 8601). Kuni 1000 kirjet. |\n"
"| `set_literal` | object | Nagu set, kuid väärtuses olevad looksulud on tekst, mitte muutujad. |\n"
"| `counter_start` | integer | Esimese sildi `{=counter}`; see kasvab sildi sammu võrra iga sildi, koopia ja reaga. 0 kuni 999999999999999 |\n"
"| `data_rows` | array of object | Seeriasildid: üks silt rea kohta, veeru nimi -> väärtus; sildi `{Column}`-kohatäited võtavad väärtused. Arve käsitletakse tekstina, null tühja lahtrina. Kuni 100000 rida, 1000 veergu, 2000000 lahtrit, 100000 märki väärtuse kohta. |\n"
"| `data_file` | string | Või CSV-, TSV-, ODS- või XLSX-fail siltide kaustas. Ilma data_rows ja data_file kasutatakse sildi enda andmefaili, kui see asub sildi kõrval siltide kaustas. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | Andmefaili leht, vaikimisi esimene. |\n"
"| `row` | integer | Näidatav andmerida, alates 1-st. 1 kuni 100000; vaikimisi `1` |\n"
"| `format` | `\"png\"` \\| `\"json\"` | 'json': laius, kõrgus, hoiatused ja PNG base64-s. vaikimisi `\"png\"` |\n"
"| `view` | `\"preview\"` \\| `\"printer\"` | 'printer': pilt sellisena, nagu printer selle saab (pööratult, oma värvides). vaikimisi `\"preview\"` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | PNG, or JSON with format=json. Warning codes also in the header X-Tavletta-Warnings (comma-separated). |  |\n"
"| 400 | Invalid request | `bad_request`, `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `no_label`, `data_conflict`, `data_column`, `not_json`, `no_rows`, `no_data`, `no_printer`, `too_many_copies` |\n"
"| 404 | No such label, printer or data file | `label_not_found`, `printer_not_found`, `data_not_found` |\n"
"| 413 | Too large: body, data rows or the label to render | `too_large`, `label_too_large` |\n"
"| 422 | The label or its data cannot be used | `file_problem`, `label_not_label`, `label_newer`, `label_damaged`, `label_unprintable`, `data_outside`, `data_problem`, `prepare_failed` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | PNG või JSON, kui format=json. Hoiatuskoodid ka päises X-Tavletta-Warnings (komadega eraldatud). |  |\n"
"| 400 | Vigane päring | `bad_request`, `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `no_label`, `data_conflict`, `data_column`, `not_json`, `no_rows`, `no_data`, `no_printer`, `too_many_copies` |\n"
"| 404 | Sellist silti, printerit või andmefaili pole | `label_not_found`, `printer_not_found`, `data_not_found` |\n"
"| 413 | Liiga suur: keha, andmeread või renderdatav silt | `too_large`, `label_too_large` |\n"
"| 422 | Silti või selle andmeid ei saa kasutada | `file_problem`, `label_not_label`, `label_newer`, `label_damaged`, `label_unprintable`, `data_outside`, `data_problem`, `prepare_failed` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}], \"format\": \"png\"}' \\\n"
"     -o preview.png \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/preview\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`POST /api/v1/print` { #post-print }"
msgstr "`POST /api/v1/print` { #post-print }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid ""
"Print: the request is checked, then queued; each printer prints one job at a "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Printimine: päring kontrollitakse, seejärel pannakse järjekorda; iga printer "
"prindib ühe töö korraga."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/api.md
msgid "Role: `print`"
msgstr "Roll: `print`"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field | Type | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `label` | string | Name of a label file in the labels folder (see GET /labels), subfolders with '/'; '`.tavletta`' may be left out. Either label or label_content. |\n"
"| `label_content` | object | Or the label itself, as the JSON of a `.tavletta` file, checked like a file that is opened. Its data file is ignored (send data_rows instead), its counter never saved. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | With `printers.toml` on the server: the printer's name (default: the default printer the token may use, or the only one). Without it: a printer model id, if not the label's own (the label is fitted as in the app). |\n"
"| `set` | object | Element name or variable name -> value, as `--set` on the command line; variables in a value are filled in; 'date' sets the moment `{=date}` and `{=time}` start from (ISO 8601). At most 1000 entries. |\n"
"| `set_literal` | object | Like set, but braces in a value are text, not variables. |\n"
"| `counter_start` | integer | The `{=counter}` of the first label; it goes up by the label's step with every label, copy and row. 0 to 999999999999999 |\n"
"| `data_rows` | array of object | Serial labels: one label per row, column name -> value; the label's `{Column}` placeholders take the values. Numbers are taken as text, null as an empty cell. At most 100000 rows, 1000 columns, 2000000 cells, 100000 characters a value. |\n"
"| `data_file` | string | Or a CSV, TSV, ODS or XLSX file in the labels folder. Without data_rows and data_file, the label's own data file is used if it lies beside the label in the labels folder. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | Sheet of the data file, the first by default. |\n"
"| `host` | string | Printer address, only without `printers.toml` (default: the one set in the app, else with `--discover` the only printer found). Refused (host_given) with `printers.toml`. |\n"
"| `copies` | integer | Copies of each label (each row); at most the printer's max_copies. Copies times rows: at most `--max-labels` (10000 by default), on label sheets at most 999. 1 to 9999; default `1` |\n"
"| `rows` | string | The data rows to print, from 1: '3-10', '5', '7-' (to the last) or '-4'. To print again from where a job stopped. |\n"
"| `no_save_counter` | boolean | Do not save the next `{=counter}` value into the label file. default `false` |\n"
"| `wait` | number | Seconds to wait for the job to finish before answering: 200 if it did, else 202. 0 to 300.0; default `0` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Väli | Tüüp | Tähendus |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `label` | string | Sildifaili nimi siltide kaustas (vaata GET /labels), alamkaustad märgiga '/'; '`.tavletta`' võib ära jätta. Kas label või label_content. |\n"
"| `label_content` | object | Või silt ise, `.tavletta`-faili JSON-ina, kontrollitud nagu avatav fail. Selle andmefaili ignoreeritakse (saada selle asemel data_rows), selle loendurit ei salvestata kunagi. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | Serveris oleva `printers.toml`-iga: printeri nimi (vaikimisi: vaikeprinter, mida token tohib kasutada, või ainus). Ilma selleta: printerimudeli id, kui see ei ole sildi enda oma (silt sobitatakse nagu rakenduses). |\n"
"| `set` | object | Elemendi nimi või muutuja nimi -> väärtus, nagu `--set` käsureal; väärtuses olevad muutujad täidetakse; 'date' seab hetke, millest `{=date}` ja `{=time}` alustavad (ISO 8601). Kuni 1000 kirjet. |\n"
"| `set_literal` | object | Nagu set, kuid väärtuses olevad looksulud on tekst, mitte muutujad. |\n"
"| `counter_start` | integer | Esimese sildi `{=counter}`; see kasvab sildi sammu võrra iga sildi, koopia ja reaga. 0 kuni 999999999999999 |\n"
"| `data_rows` | array of object | Seeriasildid: üks silt rea kohta, veeru nimi -> väärtus; sildi `{Column}`-kohatäited võtavad väärtused. Arve käsitletakse tekstina, null tühja lahtrina. Kuni 100000 rida, 1000 veergu, 2000000 lahtrit, 100000 märki väärtuse kohta. |\n"
"| `data_file` | string | Või CSV-, TSV-, ODS- või XLSX-fail siltide kaustas. Ilma data_rows ja data_file kasutatakse sildi enda andmefaili, kui see asub sildi kõrval siltide kaustas. |\n"
"| `sheet` | string | Andmefaili leht, vaikimisi esimene. |\n"
"| `host` | string | Printeri aadress, ainult ilma `printers.toml`-ita (vaikimisi: rakenduses seatud, muidu valikuga `--discover` ainus leitud printer). Lükatakse tagasi (host_given) koos `printers.toml`-iga. |\n"
"| `copies` | integer | Iga sildi (iga rea) koopiad; kuni printeri max_copies. Koopiad korda read: kuni `--max-labels` (vaikimisi 10000), sildilehtedel kuni 999. 1 kuni 9999; vaikimisi `1` |\n"
"| `rows` | string | Prinditavad andmeread alates 1-st: '3-10', '5', '7-' (viimaseni) või '-4'. Uuesti printimiseks sealt, kus töö peatus. |\n"
"| `no_save_counter` | boolean | Ära salvesta järgmist `{=counter}` väärtust sildifaili. vaikimisi `false` |\n"
"| `wait` | number | Sekundid, mida oodata töö lõppemist enne vastamist: 200, kui lõppes, muidu 202. 0 kuni 300,0; vaikimisi `0` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | The job finished within 'wait' |  |\n"
"| 202 | Queued or printing; follow it at Location |  |\n"
"| 400 | Invalid request | `bad_request`, `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `no_label`, `data_conflict`, `data_column`, `not_json`, `no_rows`, `no_data`, `no_printer`, `no_host`, `host_given`, `too_many_copies` |\n"
"| 404 | No such label, printer or data file, or a printer the token may not use | `label_not_found`, `printer_not_found`, `data_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | The label file is not writable: the next counter value could not be saved, nothing was printed; or it was replaced while the request was checked (label_changed): send it again | `counter_not_saved`, `label_changed` |\n"
"| 413 | Too large: body, data rows, labels in one job or the label to render | `too_large`, `too_many_labels`, `label_too_large` |\n"
"| 422 | The label would print wrongly | `file_problem`, `label_not_label`, `label_newer`, `label_damaged`, `label_unprintable`, `data_outside`, `data_problem` |\n"
"| 429 | Too many wrong tokens, or too many jobs waiting (100 in all, 20 per named token) | `too_many_requests`, `queue_full` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | Töö lõppes 'wait' jooksul |  |\n"
"| 202 | Järjekorras või prindib; jälgi seda aadressil Location |  |\n"
"| 400 | Vigane päring | `bad_request`, `invalid_field`, `unknown_field`, `no_label`, `data_conflict`, `data_column`, `not_json`, `no_rows`, `no_data`, `no_printer`, `no_host`, `host_given`, `too_many_copies` |\n"
"| 404 | Sellist silti, printerit või andmefaili pole, või printer, mida token ei tohi kasutada | `label_not_found`, `printer_not_found`, `data_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | Sildifaili ei saa kirjutada: loenduri järgmist väärtust ei saanud salvestada, midagi ei prinditud; või see asendati päringu kontrollimise ajal (label_changed): saada uuesti | `counter_not_saved`, `label_changed` |\n"
"| 413 | Liiga suur: keha, andmeread, sildid ühes töös või renderdatav silt | `too_large`, `too_many_labels`, `label_too_large` |\n"
"| 422 | Silt prinditaks valesti | `file_problem`, `label_not_label`, `label_newer`, `label_damaged`, `label_unprintable`, `data_outside`, `data_problem` |\n"
"| 429 | Liiga palju valesid tokeneid või liiga palju ootavaid töid (100 kokku, 20 nimetatud tokeni kohta) | `too_many_requests`, `queue_full` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"asset-tag\", \"printer\": \"it-cab\", \"data_rows\": [{\"AssetNumber\": \"100001\"}], \"wait\": 30}' \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/print\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`GET /api/v1/jobs/{id}` { #get-jobs-id }"
msgstr "`GET /api/v1/jobs/{id}` { #get-jobs-id }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid ""
"State of a print job (a print token: its own jobs; admin: all). Kept 24 "
"hours after it finished."
msgstr ""
"Printimistöö olek (print-token: oma tööd; admin: kõik). Hoitakse 24 tundi "
"pärast lõppemist."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Parameter | In | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `id` | path | The id of POST /print. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Parameeter | Asukoht | Tähendus |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `id` | path | POST /print päringu id. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | Job |  |\n"
"| 404 | No such job | `job_not_found` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 200 | Töö |  |\n"
"| 404 | Sellist tööd pole | `job_not_found` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/jobs/$JOB\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DELETE /api/v1/jobs/{id}` { #delete-jobs-id }"
msgstr "`DELETE /api/v1/jobs/{id}` { #delete-jobs-id }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
msgid ""
"Cancel a job: at once while it waits, after the labels already sent to the "
"printer while it prints (cab: the job of up to labels_per_job labels)."
msgstr ""
"Töö tühistamine: kohe, kui see ootab, printerisse juba saadetud siltide "
"järel, kui see prindib (cab: kuni labels_per_job sildiga töö)."

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Answer | Codes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 202 | Canceled, or stopping after the labels already sent |  |\n"
"| 404 | No such job | `job_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | Already finished | `job_finished` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Vastus | Koodid |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| 202 | Tühistatud või peatub juba saadetud siltide järel |  |\n"
"| 404 | Sellist tööd pole | `job_not_found` |\n"
"| 409 | On juba lõppenud | `job_finished` |\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n"
"     -X DELETE \\\n"
"     \"$TAVLETTA/jobs/$JOB\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Answers { #answers }"
msgstr "Vastused { #answers }"

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job { #job }"
msgstr "Job { #job }"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/api.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field | Type | Meaning |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `id` | string | Random, 16 characters. |\n"
"| `state` | `\"queued\"` \\| `\"waiting\"` \\| `\"printing\"` \\| `\"done\"` \\| `\"failed\"` \\| `\"canceled\"` | waiting: its turn came, another job holds the label file (its counter). done, failed and canceled are final. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | Printer model id. |\n"
"| `printer_name` | string or null | Its name in `printers.toml`. |\n"
"| `host` | string | The printer's address. |\n"
"| `owner` | string or null | Name of the token. |\n"
"| `label` | string or null | Name in the labels folder; null for label_content. |\n"
"| `printed` | integer | Labels printed so far, for certain; rises label by label while the job prints, as far as the printer tells. |\n"
"| `printed_max` | integer or null | After a failure whose outcome the printer could not tell (the connection was lost while it printed): up to this many labels may have printed. The counter goes on after them; rows_printed counts the rows printed for certain, so printing again from the next one may print labels twice. null otherwise. |\n"
"| `total` | integer | Labels to print: copies x rows. |\n"
"| `rows_printed` | integer | Data rows printed in full: after a failure, print again with rows set to the next one (rows_printed + first row). |\n"
"| `cancel_requested` | boolean | DELETE was sent. |\n"
"| `error` | null or Warning | Why it failed: `printer_<code>`, counter_not_saved, label_locked or prepare_failed. |\n"
"| `remark` | string or null | A note of the printer, for people. |\n"
"| `warnings` | array of Warning | Found when it was checked; it printed anyway. other_labels_loaded: the printer reports other labels loaded than the label's (their size, or the label distance it measured); for a printer of `printers.toml` as in a preview when the job is queued, and replaced by what the printer reports when the job prints, if it then tells of the loaded labels. |\n"
"| `created` | string | UTC. |\n"
"| `started` | string or null |  |\n"
"| `finished` | string or null |  |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Väli | Tüüp | Tähendus |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `id` | string | Juhuslik, 16 märki. |\n"
"| `state` | `\"queued\"` \\| `\"waiting\"` \\| `\"printing\"` \\| `\"done\"` \\| `\"failed\"` \\| `\"canceled\"` | waiting: tema kord on tulnud, teine töö hoiab sildifaili (selle loendurit). done, failed ja canceled on lõplikud. |\n"
"| `printer` | string | Printerimudeli id. |\n"
"| `printer_name` | string or null | Selle nimi failis `printers.toml`. |\n"
"| `host` | string | Printeri aadress. |\n"
"| `owner` | string or null | Tokeni nimi. |\n"
"| `label` | string or null | Nimi siltide kaustas; null väljal label_content. |\n"
"| `printed` | integer | Seni prinditud sildid, kindlasti; kasvab silt-silt haaval, kui töö prindib, niivõrd kui printer teatab. |\n"
"| `printed_max` | integer or null | Pärast tõrget, mille tulemust printer ei osanud öelda (ühendus katkes printimise ajal): kuni nii palju silte võib olla prinditud. Loendur jätkub nende järel; rows_printed loeb kindlasti prinditud read, nii et järgmisest reast uuesti printimine võib printida silte kaks korda. Muidu null. |\n"
"| `total` | integer | Prinditavad sildid: koopiad x read. |\n"
"| `rows_printed` | integer | Täielikult prinditud andmeread: pärast ebaõnnestumist prindi uuesti, kus rows on järgmine (rows_printed + esimene rida). |\n"
"| `cancel_requested` | boolean | DELETE saadeti. |\n"
"| `error` | null or Warning | Miks ebaõnnestus: `printer_<code>`, counter_not_saved, label_locked või prepare_failed. |\n"
"| `remark` | string or null | Printeri märkus inimestele. |\n"
"| `warnings` | array of Warning | Leitud kontrollimisel; prinditi siiski. other_labels_loaded: printer teatab, et sinna on laaditud teised sildid kui sildil (nende suurus või mõõdetud siltidevaheline kaugus); `printers.toml`-i printeri jaoks nagu eelvaates töö järjekorda panemisel ja asendatakse sellega, mida printer töö printimisel teatab, kui ta siis laaditud siltidest teatab. |\n"
"| `created` | string | UTC. |\n"
"| `started` | string or null |  |\n"
"| `finished` | string or null |  |\n"

